          "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0"
        ],
        "text": "Full speed ahead. NVIDIA’s juggernaut has passed Team Turducken, and the climb toward the two strongholds continues. Jean-François Puget and his NVARC3 teammates hold fourth on 56.26 this morning, with Turducken close behind on 56.02. Above them, Yi-Chia Chen and Tufa Labs still command the heights. Can they withstand the siege?"
      },
      {
        "heading": "The road from eighth to fourth",
        "sourceIds": [
          "board",
          "fact-15770880-0",
          "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0",
          "person-ivan-sorokin-identity-0"
        ],
        "text": "Saturday’s NVIDIA seven were eighth on 49.89. Sunday brought the big advance: 56.15, four places gained, and the pass on Turducken. Monday’s extra 0.11 takes NVARC3 to 56.26 and stretches that narrow advantage to 0.24. The juggernaut has been climbing all weekend.\n\nPuget and Ivan Sorokin won the 2025 ARC Prize together as NVARC. Now they are part of a seven-account NVARC3 crew. The next place up the mountain belongs to xz, third on 58.59: a further 2.33 points away."
      },
      {
        "heading": "The strongholds hold—for now",
        "sourceIds": [
          "board"
        ],
        "text": "Yi-Chia Chen @ Fields Model leads on 75.56; Tufa Labs follows on 70.24. Neither has added to that score overnight. Chen’s advantage is 5.32, and Tufa still has 11.65 points over xz. There is plenty of mountain between the leaders and the machines below.\n\nThe pressure is growing farther down. Grigoriy Zatravkin & co has climbed from 50.48 to 54.55, taking sixth. The last dance has improved from 51.51 to 54.52 and sits seventh, just 0.03 behind Grigoriy. Turducken’s cushion over sixth is now 1.47."
      },
      {
        "heading": "A leap out of the pack",
        "sourceIds": [
          "board"
        ],
        "text": "Then there is infinity. A jump from 31.24 to 53.12 carried the team from 593rd to sixth in one board reading overnight. Grigoriy and the last dance have since moved ahead, leaving infinity eighth—but still inside the top ten after starting the night hundreds of places away.\n\nMd Boktiar Mahbub Murad reaches 47.29 and eleventh; The ARChitects rises to 47.19 and twelfth. The gold cutoff is now 41.73 at twentieth. The two strongholds may be standing still, but the field beneath them is anything but settled."
      },
      {
        "sourceIds": [
          "fact-15605182-0"
        ],
        "text": "Disclosure: ARC Daily Digest editor Mark Barney competes on Team Turducken."
      }
    ],
